# Cairn environment variables
#
# Good news: this app needs NO paid API keys. Every integrated source
# (Hugging Face, arXiv, GitHub, Zenodo, Semantic Scholar, data.gov, OpenML,
# Kaggle) works anonymously out of the box.
#
# The variables below are OPTIONAL overrides. Defaults are in parentheses.

# Where the SQLite cache lives (default: .cairn/cache.db in the project root;
# on Vercel it automatically uses the ephemeral /tmp).
# CAIRN_CACHE_PATH=.cairn/cache.db
# DATAFORGE_CACHE_PATH=.dataforge/cache.db   # legacy alias, still honoured

# Optional: Hugging Face read token. Only needed to see *gated* repos or to
# raise anonymous rate limits. https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# HF_TOKEN=

# Optional: GitHub token. GitHub's search API allows 60 anonymous requests/hr,
# but 5,000/hr with a token. When unset the app works anonymously and shows a
# "rate-limited" chip instead of failing once the hourly budget is gone.
# https://github.com/settings/tokens
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kaggle (shared key, optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you set BOTH of these, Cairn offers Kaggle in the source dropdown and
# searches it for everyone using this shared quota. Kaggle does NOT publish
# numeric rate limits, so Cairn tracks its own conservative budget
# (KAGGLE_SHARED_BUDGET requests per KAGGLE_SHARED_WINDOW_MIN minutes) and,
# at ~75% of it, calmly asks users to connect their own Kaggle account
# instead of failing. Users can always connect their own key themselves,
# which bypasses this shared quota entirely.
# https://www.kaggle.com/settings -> API (legacy)
# KAGGLE_USERNAME=
# KAGGLE_KEY=
# KAGGLE_SHARED_BUDGET=120
# KAGGLE_SHARED_WINDOW_MIN=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq (optional — powers "Discuss" mode + AI Insight)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a Groq key, Cairn still works: Basic mode needs no AI, and the
# Discuss/AI Insight features quietly stay off.
# https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=
#
# Model for all Groq calls. The free-tier default (llama-3.1-8b-instant)
# allows ~14,400 requests/day. Set GROQ_MODEL to a higher-quality model (e.g.
# llama-3.3-70b-versatile) if your key has room.
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
#
# Max AI Insight generations per day across all users (default: 50).
# AI_INSIGHT_DAILY_CAP=50